## Frick today
Nothing — store lookup is pure app glue.

## What RangerCRM built
/Users/bri/dev/RangerCRM/RangerCRM/Model/RangerData/Migration/DataController+FrickStoresBridge.swift — 127 lines of mechanical KeyPath plumbing, e.g.
```swift
extension DataController {
    @MainActor var accounts: [AccountFrickModel] { FrickAccountStore.bridge?.accounts ?? [] }
    // ... ~20 more, identical shape
}
```
plus the `static weak var bridge: Frick<Entity>Store?` set in each store's init.

## What the port gives us
A generic, type-keyed store registry in FrickSwift (resolve the live store/array for a given Model type) so @FrickQuery and any consumer can find a store without an app-owned DataController exposing hand-written KeyPaths. The bridge file disappears entirely.

## Notes
Coupled with the FrickStore story (the `bridge` pointer is the seed of this) and a hard dependency for re-anchoring @FrickQuery off RangerCRM's DataController. Largely falls out of the store work — track separately so the @FrickQuery port has a clean anchor to depend on.
